My previous posting seems to look ok, so I'm trying to make another one on a
different topic. Ever since the first time I used nethack, I got irritated at
the way I always ended up picking heavy things I did not need nor want, either
by mistake or because the computer was slow (ie I typed hhhh, thought perhaps
that gummy keyboard had taken just hh, sent 2 extra hh and got a bonus kobold
corpse with the message being quickly replaced by "ouch, you bump into a
door"). The problem is (1) the extra keystrokes to dump the thing you didn't
want, and (2) the possible "real" problems ensuing from the lost turns or chest
carried because you didn't realize you had picked it up (in a hill orc
battlefield, this can happen quite easily :-) ).

Basically what I would love to have is a third pickup option, in addition to
manual and automatic: selective pickup of anything which isn't a corpse and
isn't heavy (I *do* definitely want to pickup food rations automatically!). In
this mode, I would like to pick up anything but corpses, chests, statues,
boulders and rocks by just moving onto it; the program would display everything
I haven't taken as it does in 'PICKUP: OFF' mode, and I would have the option to
get that stuff with the normal ',' command if I want to.

While I'm on the subject of pickup, another nice thing inside the shops would
be a price tag on the message that tells you what is on the floor there. I
always find it inconvenient to have to pick up an object to know the price, and
then drop it if I don't want it. In one occasion this inconvenience was fatal,
as the character in question had a cursed ring of teleportation which decided
to fire off right at this time (and that was PL2, the shopkeeper did NOT kindly
inquire whether you might have happened to forget to pay if he found you in the
middle of the Kops battlefield...)

